Translation patch: the flags types `StatusFlags`, `CapabilityFlags`, `CursorType`, `StmtExecuteParamsFlags`, `StmtExecuteParamFlags`, `ColumnFlags`

Change: A new macro `my_plain_bitflags!` (src/bitflags_ext.rs) takes the same input as `my_bitflags!` but, instead of calling `bitflags::bitflags!`, defines the flags type as `#[repr(transparent)] struct Name(T)` and writes out the API that `bitflags` 2.13 generates for it: the flag constants, `empty`, `all`, `bits`, `from_bits`, `from_bits_truncate`, `from_bits_retain`, `from_name`, `is_empty`, `is_all`, `intersects`, `contains`, `insert`, `remove`, `toggle`, `set`, `intersection`, `union`, `difference`, `symmetric_difference`, `complement`, `iter`, `iter_names`, `impl bitflags::Flags`, `Debug`, `Binary`/`Octal`/`LowerHex`/`UpperHex`, `BitOr`/`BitAnd`/`BitXor`/`Sub`/`Not` and the `*Assign` forms, `Extend`, `FromIterator`, `IntoIterator`. The six flags types used by the translated code switch to it, and drop `Debug` from their `derive` list (the macro writes the `bitflags` one). The macro's `TryFrom<T>` is `match Name::from_bits(val) { Some(flags) => Ok(flags), None => Err(Error(val)) }` instead of `Name::from_bits(val).ok_or_else(|| Error(val))`.
Why: `bitflags!` wraps a private `InternalBitFlags` whose methods go through the external `bitflags::Bits`/`Flags` traits (`Bits::EMPTY`, `Bits::ALL`, a `const` fold over `Flags::FLAGS`), which Aeneas has no model for. A plain struct over `T` with primitive bit operations translates directly. (`ok_or_else` with a closure: see patch 09.)
Behaviour: Identical. Each method body is the one in `bitflags` 2.13.2 (`src/public.rs`, `src/internal.rs`) with the internal wrapper inlined (`self.0` is the bits in both). `all()` is the OR of all flag values, which is what `bitflags` computes by folding over `FLAGS`. `Flags::FLAGS` lists the same (name, value) pairs in the same order, so `iter`, `iter_names`, `from_name` and the `Debug` output (`Name(A | B | 0x..)`, or `Name(0x0)` when empty, through `bitflags::parser::to_writer`) are unchanged. The derived `PartialEq`/`Eq`/`Hash`/`Clone`/`Copy` work on the bits, as before. `match` is the definition of `ok_or_else`. Not generated: the `FromStr`/`Display`/`AsRef` impls of the private internal type, and `bitflags::__private::PublicFlags`. None of these is reachable from the public type, and the crate compiles with all features.

